{
	"version": 1,
	"_help": "Weapon attachments (Skillz). Bought once with Gravemark (account-wide unlock), then equipped per weapon archetype: every weapon of that archetype uses the archetype's loadout. classes[archetype].slots = slots it has (DESI_ATTACHMENTS.md §1); optic_cap limits optic size (micro<short<mid<long). attachment.classes = optional allow list (default: every class with that slot). tier 1/2/3: equipping needs the weapon's upgrade tier >= tier_requires[tier] (0/2/4). mods (WeaponItem, multiply unless *_add): damage_mult rpm_mult mag_mult reload_mult (time) spread_mult (all fire) hip_spread_mult (not ADS) recoil_mult range_mult (falloff start) swap_mult (time) pellets_add headshot_add reserve_mags_add. ads (AdsProfile): fov (ADS FOV cap: aimed FOV = min(class FOV x fov_mult, fov), never widens) fov_mult (x the class iron-sight FOV) move_mult spread_mult (multiply the ADS penalties) ads_time_mult sway_mult (x the class ADS time / sway). optic = optics lineup block on optic-slot parts (Armory.optic_profile). art_pending = [model, icon] not shipped yet (default sight picture / glyph until they land). flags = presentation hooks for player.gd/HUD (tracer_hidden, flash_mult, scope_overlay, outline_elites, heartbeat_counter, bipod, flashlight, mine_lamp). effects = SkillEffect defs (same format as skill_tree.json) run by the player's SkillRunner only while a weapon of that archetype is in hand. slots[].hides = default gun meshes (Desi split guns) a fitted part hides; an attachment \"hides\" overrides it ([] = hide nothing); \"hides_by_class\" {archetype: [...]} overrides both for that archetype (Sawn Stub on the shotgun also hides IronSights + the DefaultMag tube); \"inner_hides\" {archetype or \"*\": [node names]} hides nodes inside the part itself on that host (Sawn Stub's MagTubeStub shows on the shotgun only). exclusions = per-archetype parts that can't be equipped together ({id, classes, parts, reason}; Armory.exclusion_reason); a save holding one unequips the last listed part on load (it stays owned). Flashlight parts (mine_lamp, lantern_rail; F toggles the beam) carry light_energy / light_range / light_angle / light_attenuation / light_color for the camera SpotLight3D (Armory.flashlight_config).",
